data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"A GPU in a tensor-parallel group holds a share of everything: a slice of each weight matrix and the KV heads it\nserves. Ask what a share costs for each part, and what the GPU can actually use after a reserve. The answer is the\nsmallest group size whose share of the weights plus its share of the cache plus its workspace fits in that budget."},"hints_note":null}

