data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Compute the usable bytes first: memory times the unreserved percent, floored. Then, for each allowed degree, add three\nper-GPU terms: the weight bytes divided by the degree, rounded up; the KV bytes for all the tokens of all sequences,\ndivided by the degree; and the workspace. The degrees are powers of two, and a degree is allowed only when it divides the\nnumber of KV heads. The first allowed degree whose total is at most the usable bytes is the answer."},"hints_note":null}

